# ============================================================
# Login.gov CRM migration pipeline - ignore rules
# ============================================================
# THIS FILE MUST TRAVEL WITH THIS FOLDER. It is not a duplicate of the
# engineering repo's root .gitignore - it is the copy that keeps working after
# this folder is dropped into the GSA Salesforce Operations repository, where
# that root .gitignore does not exist.
#
# Git applies a .gitignore to the directory containing it and everything below,
# in whatever repository that directory happens to sit in. So these rules hold
# in the engineering repo today and in the Operations repo tomorrow, with no
# action required from whoever does the move.
#
# WHAT IS BEING PROTECTED. Running this pipeline writes real Login.gov partner
# and applicant data to disk: names, email addresses, agency contacts, partner
# notes. It lands in data/ (pulled from Airtable, and staged for the Bulk API)
# and in logs/ (transcripts, review CSVs, and the Bulk API's own failure rows,
# which echo the full record payload). NONE of it may be committed - to this
# repository or to any other.
#
# If you are adding a new output location to the pipeline, add it here in the
# same change. An output folder that nobody thought about is how PII gets
# committed.

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Credentials
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# .env holds the Airtable Personal Access Token. .env.example holds no secrets
# and is the template operators copy, so it is the one file here that IS
# tracked - see docs/SETUP.md.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Run output - transcripts, review CSVs, summaries, restore points
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Folder structure is kept (via .gitkeep) so a fresh clone can run without
# creating directories by hand; the contents are not.
logs/**
!logs/**/
!logs/**/.gitkeep
!logs/**/README.md

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Data - Airtable extracts, load-ready CSVs, the production Account export
# ------------------------------------------------------------
data/**
!data/**/
!data/**/.gitkeep
!data/**/README.md

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Salesforce CLI bulk job result files
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# `sf data bulk results` writes these into the CURRENT WORKING DIRECTORY rather
# than anywhere this pipeline chooses, so they can appear next to the scripts
# themselves. They contain full record payloads.
750*-success-records.csv
750*-failed-records.csv

# Salesforce CLI local state, if `sf` is ever run from inside this folder.
.sf/
.sfdx/
**/*.sfdx-token

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# OS and editor junk
# ------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
[Dd]esktop.ini
